## Opening

This is the first chapter, so it opens the whole video. Begin with an opening of about two hundred words, counted within the target, that follows this shape.
1. A cold open built on a concrete, relatable moment or a strange true fact. Never start with a greeting.
2. The central question of the video, stated simply.
3. A gentle roadmap naming two or three specific things we will explore, without revealing the answers.
4. A calm settling-in moment that ends with the channel name.
Then flow naturally into the chapter content.

Example of the shape, for structure and tone only. Do not reuse its sentences, its opening words, or its topic.

"When you were seven years old, one summer lasted forever. The days stretched out like warm taffy. You had time to get bored, to build a fort, to forget about the fort, and to build another one. Then, somewhere along the way, summers started slipping by like a long weekend. A whole year now passes in the time it used to take to wait for your birthday.

Ask anyone over forty, and they will nod slowly. But the clocks have not changed. A minute is still sixty seconds. So where did all that time go?

Tonight, we are going to follow that question gently, one step at a time. We will meet a scientist who lived in a cave for two months without a clock. We will step inside the brain and find the tiny moments it chooses to keep, and the ones it quietly lets go. And by the end, we will find a few surprising ways to make time stretch out again.

So get comfortable. Let your shoulders drop. There is no rush tonight. This is Sleepy Mind Lab, and we have all the time in the world."
